hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17719","Waki narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Dukayn ibn Said al-Khathami who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were four hundred and forty, asking him for food. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Stand and give them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but what sustains me in the summer and the children. Waki said: Al-qayz in the speech of the Arabs is four months. He said: Stand and give them. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, hearing and obeying. He said: So Umar stood and we stood with him, and he took us up to a room of his, and took the key out of his waist wrapper and opened the door. Dukayn said: In the room there were dates like a reclining young camel. He said: Help yourselves. He said: Each man among us took his need, whatever he wished. He said: Then I turned, while I was among the last of them, and it was as if we had taken not a date from it."
